
MVP (Minimum Viable Product) for the first version of the solution:
  ☒ Remove all service-x, service-y and existing service names from everywhere since solution is generic (not related to particular project)
  ☒ UX: analyze how to make UI more compact, usually its much more services than environments (at least 10 services), propose options by making new mockups
  ☒ UX: Usually deployment workflow for a service looks more like a tree, for instance dev could be deployed to qa-1 and qa-2, qa-2 can be deployed on uat 2 and qa-1 can be deployed on uat-1 etc.
  ☒ Add another two attributes to deployment: ref (name of branch/number of pr or commit) and sha (sha of commit), both of them are optional, we will use them later on UI.
  ☒ UX: make ability on UI to use ref and sha attributes for "Display"  and "Topology" functionality
  ☒ Architecture: There is no need for now to have separate containers for read and write API, it is still two separate components, but they can be in the same container, we can split them later if needed, for instance if read API will require more resources than write API, etc. For now we can just have one component with two separate APIs, and we can scale it as a whole, but in the future we can split it into two separate containers if needed.Write API still must require api key.
  ☒ UX: Add ability to switch to light/dark/auto theme, propose options by making new mockups
  ☒ UX: Version could be quite long (50 symbols max), but now only glance view  shows it fully and properly, despite the fact that half of the width is not used, since there is not so many envs (and in most projects their number is up to 10).
  ☐ Architecture:Define more strict and standardized API, mandatory/optional fields, field types, length, etc, and implement validation of incoming data in backend, return proper error messages if data is not valid. For instance, version could be up to 50 symbols, but we can set default max length to 20 and return error if version is longer than that, or we can allow any length but truncate it on UI and show full version in tooltip. Also we can set some standard for version format, for instance it should start with letter and can contain only letters, numbers, dots and dashes, etc. We can also add some optional fields for deployment, for instance ref (name of branch/number of pr or commit) and sha (sha of commit), both of them are optional, we will use them later on UI.Generate openapi spec and also add swagger or scalar to API app.
  ☐ Architecture: Introduce Control API, separate component in the same container as current API is, all components will be receiving commands from control API by periodical polling it and reporting status (if its inprocess then commands and statuses will be delivered immediately). Default polling interval is 30 sec, must be configurable.
  ☐ Architecture: What if there is no ability to call write API from CI/CD pipeline? Then I would add another component (with separate container) that will be responsible for fetching deployment data from CI/CD tool (for instance by calling its API) and pushing it to our backend, so we will have two options to get data to our backend: either directly from CI/CD pipeline or through this component.  This component will be optional and installed/deployed separately, it will require organization of credentials for CI/CD tool API access, and configuration of fetching period (default 30 seconds), will go to the API of CI/CD will track cursor of last fetched deployments to avoid exceeding API limits, etc, for the first time it will take first n items which is configurable also. Architecture of component will be pretty simple but extendable, each CI/CD tool will have its own implementation of fetching logic, but they will all implement the same interface, so adding new CI/CD tool support will be easy and won't require changes in other parts of the system.Create only github actions implementation as MVP, based on fetching deployments API. Write API should provide API for storing and retrieving cursor or any other state of this fetcher.

  ☐ Functionality: Add synchronization API to the control API with two modes: reconciliation and full.
  ☐ UX: Rename "Workflow rows" to "Worfklows"

Phase 2.0
☐ UX: Find a way to group/colorize/correlate deployments based on different attributes available for deployment (default as version), propose options by making new mockups, one of the options should be similar to github actions grouping of jobs by workflow, but in our case it will be grouping of deployments by this attribute
☐ UX: Add back Matrix layout (deferred from MVP — services × environments grid). MVP layout axis ships with Swim-lane + Workflow-rows only; Matrix re-added later. Re-introduces the third layout option alongside the existing two; default layout decision revisited at that time.


  

